quran[26]{c,v,t}:
  92,15,"which none shall enter except the most wicked,"
  92,16,the one who rejects (the truth) and turns away.
  92,17,The most conscious (of Allah’s command) shall be spared from it.
  92,18,(He is one) who gives his wealth (for the sake of Allah) to purify himself.
  92,19,"None has any favour upon him to be repaid,"
  92,20,"but he seeks only the pleasure of his Lord, the Most Exalted."
  92,21,"Surely, he shall soon be well-pleased (with Allah’s grace)."
  93,1,"By the morning brightness,*"
  93,2,"by the night, when it calms and covers (the daylight with its darkness),*"
  93,3,"(O Prophet!) Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor is He displeased with you."
  93,4,"Surely, whatever moment (of your Prophetic period) comes after will be far better for you than the former. (Or: The exalted station of the next life will surely be far better for you than the one in this life)."
  93,5,And surely your Lord shall give you (so much) that you will be well pleased.
  93,6,Did He not find you an orphan and sheltered you (with a graceful position)?*
  93,7,He found you lost (in His love) and guided you (to your destination).*
  93,8,He found you in need (of His support) and enriched you (with His abundant favours).*
  93,9,"So, as for the orphan, never oppress (him)."
  93,10,"And as for the beggar, never repulse (him)."
  93,11,"And as for your Lord’s blessing, proclaim (it well)."
  94,1,"Have We not expanded your breast for you (Esteemed Prophet!),*"
  94,2,"and relieved you of your burden,*"
  94,3,that weighed heavily upon your back.
  94,4,Did We not raise your remembrance for you (and exalted your name)?*
  94,5,"So, indeed, with (every) hardship comes ease."
  94,6,"Indeed, with (every) hardship comes ease."
  94,7,"So, once you have fulfilled (your duty), strive (in acts of devotion),"
  94,8,and turn to your Lord eagerly.
